\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S1}{\ignorespaces Quantitative comparison of \texttt  {RhizAeon}\xspace  and 3SEQ across the 3,200-trial Posada \& Crandall (2001) benchmark suite. Results are grouped by evolutionary regime: false positive evaluation under Gamma rate heterogeneity ($\alpha \in \{2.0, 0.5, 0.05\}$, $\rho = 0$, 1,200 trials), clock-like null controls ($\rho = 0$, 400 trials), and recombinant coalescent trials ($\rho \in \{1, 4, 16, 64\}$, 1,600 trials). Columns report the population mutation parameter ($\theta $), population recombination parameter ($\rho $), alignment-level power or FPR (\%), mean inferred event count ($\hat  {K}$), precision ($\text  {PPV}$), triad lineage attribution accuracy ($S_{\mathrm  {triad}}$), and execution runtime per alignment (ms).\relax }}{26}{table.caption.20}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:supp_posada_summary}{{S1}{26}{Quantitative comparison of \RhizAeon and 3SEQ across the 3,200-trial Posada \& Crandall (2001) benchmark suite. Results are grouped by evolutionary regime: false positive evaluation under Gamma rate heterogeneity ($\alpha \in \{2.0, 0.5, 0.05\}$, $\rho = 0$, 1,200 trials), clock-like null controls ($\rho = 0$, 400 trials), and recombinant coalescent trials ($\rho \in \{1, 4, 16, 64\}$, 1,600 trials). Columns report the population mutation parameter ($\theta $), population recombination parameter ($\rho $), alignment-level power or FPR (\%), mean inferred event count ($\hat {K}$), precision ($\text {PPV}$), triad lineage attribution accuracy ($S_{\mathrm {triad}}$), and execution runtime per alignment (ms).\relax }{table.caption.20}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {S2}{\ignorespaces Empirical operational phase envelope of \texttt  {RhizAeon}\xspace  across 1,000,000 independent continuous simulation trials. Simulations span $L \in [300, 30{,}000]$\nobreakspace  {}nt, $N \in [4, 250]$\nobreakspace  {}taxa, $d_{\mathrm  {parent}} \in [0.005, 0.35]$\nobreakspace  {}subs/site, and continuous Gamma rate variation $\alpha \in [0.2, 5.0]$ alongside strict molecular clock controls ($\alpha \ge 50$). Multi-event topologies include true nulls ($K=0$), 5'/3' terminal crossovers, intercalary conversion cassettes ($K=1$), and multi-donor / multi-event mosaicism ($K \in \{2, 3, 4\}$). Breakpoint errors report median absolute error (nt) among detected recombinant tracts.\relax }}{27}{table.caption.21}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:grand_sweep_1m_envelope}{{S2}{27}{Empirical operational phase envelope of \RhizAeon across 1,000,000 independent continuous simulation trials. Simulations span $L \in [300, 30{,}000]$~nt, $N \in [4, 250]$~taxa, $d_{\mathrm {parent}} \in [0.005, 0.35]$~subs/site, and continuous Gamma rate variation $\alpha \in [0.2, 5.0]$ alongside strict molecular clock controls ($\alpha \ge 50$). Multi-event topologies include true nulls ($K=0$), 5'/3' terminal crossovers, intercalary conversion cassettes ($K=1$), and multi-donor / multi-event mosaicism ($K \in \{2, 3, 4\}$). Breakpoint errors report median absolute error (nt) among detected recombinant tracts.\relax }{table.caption.21}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S1}{\ignorespaces Empirical aeronautical operational flight envelope, information-theoretic observability frontier, and sub-gene breakpoint precision of \texttt  {RhizAeon}\xspace  across 1,000,000 independent continuous simulation trials ($N = 4\text  {--}250$ taxa, $L = 300\text  {--}30{,}000$ nt). Panel A: Aeronautical flight operating envelope in $(d_{\mathrm  {parent}} \times L_{\mathrm  {tract}}/L)$ parameter space with continuous empirical power contours. The 50\% operational boundary (white) and 90\% certified threshold (gold) demarcate the high-confidence flight corridor from the shaded Informational Stall Zone ($M_{\mathrm  {tract}} < 3$ SNPs, $P < 1\%$, red diagonal hatching). Overlaid biological landmarks mark empirical recombinant architectures: \textit  {Streptococcus pneumoniae} PMEN1 ($d=0.08, r=0.20$), HIV-1 CRF01\_AE ($d=0.12, r=0.16$), Sarbecovirus Spike RBD ($d=0.04, r=0.035$), and Primate MHC micro-conversion ($d=0.05, r=0.07$). Panel B: Information-theoretic observability frontier as a function of informative mutations in the recombinant tract ($M_{\mathrm  {tract}}$). Power transitions sharply from $0.5\%$ at the stall horizon ($M_{\mathrm  {tract}} \le 2$ SNPs) to $52.4\%$ at $M_{\mathrm  {tract}} \in [11, 15]$, $85.5\%$ at $M_{\mathrm  {tract}} \in [26, 50]$, and achieves a $99.51\%$ saturation plateau for $M_{\mathrm  {tract}} \ge 500$ SNPs ($N = 21{,}064$ trials). The non-recombinant null false positive rate floor is controlled at $0.357\%$ (green horizontal span). Panel C: Breakpoint spatial resolution error $|\hat  {u} - u^*|$ across matched events as a function of tract mutations $M_{\mathrm  {tract}}$. Median spatial error decreases monotonically from $20.0$\nobreakspace  {}nt at $M_{\mathrm  {tract}} = 6$ down to $5.0$\nobreakspace  {}nt at $M_{\mathrm  {tract}} \ge 500$ SNPs, with interquartile precision (shaded ribbon) bounded within the sub-15 nt gene margin (dotted reference line).\relax }}{28}{figure.caption.22}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:grand_sweep_1m_phase_diagram}{{S1}{28}{Empirical aeronautical operational flight envelope, information-theoretic observability frontier, and sub-gene breakpoint precision of \RhizAeon across 1,000,000 independent continuous simulation trials ($N = 4\text {--}250$ taxa, $L = 300\text {--}30{,}000$ nt). Panel A: Aeronautical flight operating envelope in $(d_{\mathrm {parent}} \times L_{\mathrm {tract}}/L)$ parameter space with continuous empirical power contours. The 50\% operational boundary (white) and 90\% certified threshold (gold) demarcate the high-confidence flight corridor from the shaded Informational Stall Zone ($M_{\mathrm {tract}} < 3$ SNPs, $P < 1\%$, red diagonal hatching). Overlaid biological landmarks mark empirical recombinant architectures: \textit {Streptococcus pneumoniae} PMEN1 ($d=0.08, r=0.20$), HIV-1 CRF01\_AE ($d=0.12, r=0.16$), Sarbecovirus Spike RBD ($d=0.04, r=0.035$), and Primate MHC micro-conversion ($d=0.05, r=0.07$). Panel B: Information-theoretic observability frontier as a function of informative mutations in the recombinant tract ($M_{\mathrm {tract}}$). Power transitions sharply from $0.5\%$ at the stall horizon ($M_{\mathrm {tract}} \le 2$ SNPs) to $52.4\%$ at $M_{\mathrm {tract}} \in [11, 15]$, $85.5\%$ at $M_{\mathrm {tract}} \in [26, 50]$, and achieves a $99.51\%$ saturation plateau for $M_{\mathrm {tract}} \ge 500$ SNPs ($N = 21{,}064$ trials). The non-recombinant null false positive rate floor is controlled at $0.357\%$ (green horizontal span). Panel C: Breakpoint spatial resolution error $|\hat {u} - u^*|$ across matched events as a function of tract mutations $M_{\mathrm {tract}}$. Median spatial error decreases monotonically from $20.0$~nt at $M_{\mathrm {tract}} = 6$ down to $5.0$~nt at $M_{\mathrm {tract}} \ge 500$ SNPs, with interquartile precision (shaded ribbon) bounded within the sub-15 nt gene margin (dotted reference line).\relax }{figure.caption.22}{}}
\global\@namedef{@lastpage@}{29}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {S2}{\ignorespaces Continuous multi-event reticulation resolution, structural topology sensitivity, and multi-donor mosaic disambiguation across the 1,000,000-trial continuous simulation sweep. Panel A: Reticulation cardinality confusion matrix comparing true event count ($K_{\mathrm  {true}}$) against inferred event count ($\hat  {K}$). On true clonal nulls ($K_{\mathrm  {true}} = 0$), $99.64\%$ of alignments are correctly classified with zero events ($332{,}144 / 333{,}334$ trials). On single events ($K_{\mathrm  {true}} = 1$), exact cardinality recovery reaches $50.7\%$, with uncalled events concentrated in sub-informative tracts ($M_{\mathrm  {tract}} < 5$ SNPs). Panel B: Continuous event-level $F_1$ score resolution curves as a function of informative mutations in the recombinant tract ($M_{\mathrm  {tract}}$ on logarithmic scale), stratified across mosaic complexities $K_{\mathrm  {true}} \in \{1, 2, 3, 4\}$ with shaded 95\% bootstrap confidence ribbons. All curves converge to an asymptotic $F_1 \ge 0.80$ plateau at $M_{\mathrm  {tract}} \ge 100$ SNPs alongside high bipartite event precision ($>92.8\%\text  {--}99.0\%$). Panel C: Continuous empirical detection power as a function of relative tract length ($L_{\mathrm  {tract}}/L$) comparing Terminal Crossovers ($N = 239{,}767$) versus Intercalary Conversion Cassettes ($N = 426{,}899$). Crossovers exhibit a consistent topological power advantage ($\Delta +4\text  {--}8\%$, shaded corridor) and elevated spatial boundary fidelity (median Jaccard $J = 0.968$ vs $0.923$). Panel D: Continuous multi-donor mosaic disambiguation across $M_{\mathrm  {tract}}$, comparing single-donor chimeras ($P_1 \leftarrow P_2$) against multi-donor chimeras ($P_1 \leftarrow P_2 + P_3$). Both sensitivity and event $F_1$ score converge to complete parity at $M_{\mathrm  {tract}} \ge 50$ SNPs ($92\%\text  {--}98\%$ power, identical spatial boundary fidelity $J = 0.879$). Independent parental dipoles in metric space deconvolve multi-donor chimeras without mutual interference.\relax }}{29}{figure.caption.23}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:grand_sweep_1m_multievent}{{S2}{29}{Continuous multi-event reticulation resolution, structural topology sensitivity, and multi-donor mosaic disambiguation across the 1,000,000-trial continuous simulation sweep. Panel A: Reticulation cardinality confusion matrix comparing true event count ($K_{\mathrm {true}}$) against inferred event count ($\hat {K}$). On true clonal nulls ($K_{\mathrm {true}} = 0$), $99.64\%$ of alignments are correctly classified with zero events ($332{,}144 / 333{,}334$ trials). On single events ($K_{\mathrm {true}} = 1$), exact cardinality recovery reaches $50.7\%$, with uncalled events concentrated in sub-informative tracts ($M_{\mathrm {tract}} < 5$ SNPs). Panel B: Continuous event-level $F_1$ score resolution curves as a function of informative mutations in the recombinant tract ($M_{\mathrm {tract}}$ on logarithmic scale), stratified across mosaic complexities $K_{\mathrm {true}} \in \{1, 2, 3, 4\}$ with shaded 95\% bootstrap confidence ribbons. All curves converge to an asymptotic $F_1 \ge 0.80$ plateau at $M_{\mathrm {tract}} \ge 100$ SNPs alongside high bipartite event precision ($>92.8\%\text {--}99.0\%$). Panel C: Continuous empirical detection power as a function of relative tract length ($L_{\mathrm {tract}}/L$) comparing Terminal Crossovers ($N = 239{,}767$) versus Intercalary Conversion Cassettes ($N = 426{,}899$). Crossovers exhibit a consistent topological power advantage ($\Delta +4\text {--}8\%$, shaded corridor) and elevated spatial boundary fidelity (median Jaccard $J = 0.968$ vs $0.923$). Panel D: Continuous multi-donor mosaic disambiguation across $M_{\mathrm {tract}}$, comparing single-donor chimeras ($P_1 \leftarrow P_2$) against multi-donor chimeras ($P_1 \leftarrow P_2 + P_3$). Both sensitivity and event $F_1$ score converge to complete parity at $M_{\mathrm {tract}} \ge 50$ SNPs ($92\%\text {--}98\%$ power, identical spatial boundary fidelity $J = 0.879$). Independent parental dipoles in metric space deconvolve multi-donor chimeras without mutual interference.\relax }{figure.caption.23}{}}
